"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe subject matter was good, but the density of the composition and the foreshadowing laid out in advance are too weak.\n\nIn particular, the  motif is too flimsy and forced.  \nThe criteria for being discovered cannot be clear.  \nHow much of the body is allowed? Does it only apply to discovery in the macroscopic world? Where does that person end?  \nIt seems better not to use such elements.  \n\nThe female protagonist is a typical villain. A very frustrating character.\n\nI wonder if the ending scene really had to be included."